5417] [17592186425539 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f954b4ca-ba90-55e4-8907-f07c9675da77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425540 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425540 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225125" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425540 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425540 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.8)$ given below, compute $P(1\\le X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0001\\,$ | $\\,0.0016\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0989\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.7379\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425540 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "39452c92-9de3-5f42-bbde-2d7fa0b6b73d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425540 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(0) \\\\  & =1.0000-0.0001 \\\\  & =0.9999.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425541 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425541 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225192" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425541 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425541 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(7,0.48)$ given below, compute $P(X>5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0103\\,$ | $\\,0.0767\\,$ | $\\,0.2607\\,$ | $\\,0.5437\\,$ | $\\,0.8049\\,$ | $\\,0.9496\\,$ | $\\,0.9941\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(X>5)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425541 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3dbd9a46-63be-542a-8056-c34929af9e15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425541 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>5) & =1-P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =1-F(5) \\\\  & =1-0.9496 \\\\  & =0.0504.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425542 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425542 #edb/ref 1069 "q-224505" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425542 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425542 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.65).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing value in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $0.0018$ | $0.0223$ | $0.1174$ | $0.3529$ | $0.6809$ | {{field-1}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425542 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "45075cea-f15c-5084-914d-ebb143f8bab5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425542 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=6$ and $p=0.65.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =0.6809+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5})(0.65)^{5}(1-0.65)^{6-5} \\\\  & =0.6809+6\\cdot (0.65)^{5}\\cdot (0.35)^{1} \\\\  & ≈0.9246.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425543 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425543 #edb/ref 1069 "q-224517" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425543 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425543 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(7,0.85)$ given below, compute $P(X<5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0000\\,$ | $\\,0.0001\\,$ | $\\,0.0012\\,$ | $\\,0.0121\\,$ | $\\,0.0738\\,$ | $\\,0.2834\\,$ | $\\,0.6794\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425543 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "84b86fdf-72f2-5ecd-9ec1-a3a6650f805e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425543 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(4) \\\\  & =0.0738.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425544 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425544 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225123" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425544 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425544 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.63)$ given below, compute $P(2<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0069\\,$ | $\\,0.0660\\,$ | $\\,0.2670\\,$ | $\\,0.6093\\,$ | $\\,0.9008\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(2<X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425544 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "af275350-4175-5761-af0d-7b660329cfde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425544 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(2<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(2<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(2) \\\\  & =1.0000-0.2670 \\\\  & =0.7330.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425545 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425545 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225190" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425545 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425545 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.79)$ given below, compute $P(X>3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0004\\,$ | $\\,0.0081\\,$ | $\\,0.0659\\,$ | $\\,0.2833\\,$ | $\\,0.6923\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425545 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6ff4041-b681-52c7-96bc-3e966d10e527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425545 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-0.2833 \\\\  & =0.7167.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425546 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425546 #edb/ref 1069 "q-224526" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425546 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425546 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.48)$ given below, compute $P(X=3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0198\\,$ | $\\,0.1293\\,$ | $\\,0.3820\\,$ | $\\,0.6930\\,$ | $\\,0.9083\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(X=3)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425546 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c7cc6a15-4009-5db6-878e-1743f9fb14e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425546 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X=3) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(X=3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =F(3)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.6930-0.3820 \\\\  & =0.3110.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
